## Interface: 50500, 50502, 50503, 50504
# 50504 is the newest of these and the one the client is on. There is no
# 50505: it was listed here for three days, and CurseForge -- unable to
# match it to any WoW version -- published the addon as supporting 3.80.2,
# which is a real interface number (38002) belonging to a different
# client entirely. An invented version does not fail, it resolves to
# somebody else's.
#
# Checked against what is installed rather than reasoned about: every
# third-party addon in the AddOns folder -- AtlasLoot, Auctionator,
# Bagnon, Bartender4 -- tops out at 50504, and not one names 50505.
## Title: ArenaPlus Data
## Author: David / Atlas-Engine
## Version: 2026.09.01.0105
## Notes: The ladder, cutoffs, specs and gear that ArenaPlus reads. Refreshed on its own so the addon itself does not have to be republished for it.
# CurseForge's own number for the project, which is what identifies it
# everywhere outside the website -- the packaging webhook posts to
# /api/projects/1672414/package, and addon managers use it to match an
# installed folder back to the project it came from.
## X-Curse-Project-ID: 1672414
# The GitHub repository CurseForge builds this from.
#
# The upload is not done by any workflow here and no API key is involved:
# the project on CurseForge is linked to this repository, and it builds a file
# the moment it sees a new tag. This line records that link where somebody
# reading the addon can see it.
## X-Curse-Repository-ID: https://github.com/Atlas-Engine/ArenaPlus_Data

# Nothing here is hand-written. Every file is produced by the scripts in
# ArenaPlus\tools\ and overwritten wholesale on the next run.
#
# Order matters only in that the cutoffs are small and read first.
Cutoffs-us.lua
Cutoffs-eu.lua
Leaderboard-us.lua
Leaderboard-eu.lua
Specs-us.lua
Specs-eu.lua
Inspect-us.lua
Inspect-eu.lua
